.po 1i
.TH SETENV 1C UCB
.V 08/15/84 17:03:48
.\" @[$]setenv.1C	1.7 08/15/84 17:03:49 - Zilog Inc.
.ad
.SH NAME
setenv \- establish or revise an environment variable
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsetenv\fI [name value]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The command 
.BI setenv " name value"
\fRSets the value of the environment variable
.I name
to be
.I value,
a single string.
Useful environment variables are TERM, the type of terminal, and
SHELL, the shell being used.
.SH SEE ALSO
csh(1), env(1), printenv(1), set(1C), unsetenv(1C).
.br
\fIThe C Shell\fR in the ZEUS Utilities Manual.
